WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.860
A tsunami begins when a disturbance rapidly moves a large volume

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.120
of water. Vertical seafloor displacement during megathrust rupture is a major

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.800
mechanism. Before rupture, a locked interface lets the overriding plate deform.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.540
When it slips, the seafloor can change shape abruptly and displace

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:21.200
the overlying water. Landslides entering water or moving underwater can also

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.820
generate tsunamis. Volcanic explosions and collapse, as in the Krakatau example,

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.680
can displace water without requiring a megathrust.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.940
In deep water, a tsunami can travel very fast with a

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.520
long wavelength and modest height.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.880
It affects a much deeper water column than an ordinary wind

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:41.580
wave. In shallow water it slows, its wavelength shortens, and its

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.840
height can increase. Coastal shape and bathymetry influence the eventual runup

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.440
and flooding. A tsunami is often a series of surges and

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.160
strong currents, not one picturesque breaking wave.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.160
An initial withdrawal of the sea can occur, but not every

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.100
tsunami begins with visible withdrawal.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.900
The 1960 Chile event produced a tsunami that crossed the Pacific

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.640
and damaged Hawaii and Japan.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.900
A community far from the earthquake can still face a tsunami.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.120
Coastal inundation can destroy buildings, move boats inland, and carry debris.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:14.940
Large landslide-generated local waves can also arrive very quickly.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.620
Warning systems combine earthquake information with sea-level and ocean-bottom measurements.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.260
Detection and forecasting support warnings;

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.160
they do not predict the exact earthquake before it begins.
